    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6">

                <pb facs="0019" n="5" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg5"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Conference W And PW/1–1245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Peru</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >White</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lima</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-12T17:00:00-05:00">January 12, 1945—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:30 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>42. When conveying message contained in Department’s circular telegram January
                    11, 7 p.m., this morning Foreign Office informed that agenda mentioned in
                    Mexican invitation to conference received here corresponded exactly with that in
                    Department’s circular January 5, 3 p.m.</p>
                <pb facs="0020" n="6" xml:id="pg6"/>
                <p>Secretary General<anchor n="6" xml:id="d6-f1"/> has now telephoned that his
                    Government approves this agenda without additional suggestions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">White</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d6-f1" n="6" xml:id="d6-f1-content">
                <p>Javier Correa, Secretary General of the Peruvian Foreign Office.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
